{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_5","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc 'rg -n \"archiveEntries|archiveTurns|derivedArchiveViews|ArchiveFinalizationService|archive-api|turn-derivation|derived-archive-view|green-verify|verify-all\" -S docs/spec-build/v2/epics/07--archive-and-derived-views/artifacts/epic/00*-epic-verifier-batch.json'","aggregated_output":"docs/spec-build/v2/epics/07--archive-and-derived-views/artifacts/epic/002-epic-verifier-batch.json:1:{\"command\":\"epic-verify\",\"version\":1,\"status\":\"blocked\",\"outcome\":\"block\",\"result\":{\"outcome\":\"block\",\"verifierResults\":[{\"resultId\":\"2f84684a-a0cf-4ae8-bc51-e485762f54fb\",\"outcome\":\"block\",\"provider\":\"codex\",\"model\":\"gpt-5.4\",\"reviewerLabel\":\"epic-verifier-1\",\"crossStoryFindings\":[\"The archive primitive, turn derivation, and derived-view layers are implemented against the full Epic 7 taxonomy, but the live execution/finalization path still feeds them legacy `ProcessHistoryItem` data, so later stories are validated against seeded archive rows instead of the real runtime source.\",\"Story 6 provenance enrichment is disconnected from Stories 2-3 production writes: archive reads can enrich `relatedArtifactVersionId` and `relatedSourceProvenanceId`, but the shipped append paths never persist those IDs.\",\"The archive page, turn page, and derived-view page all work when archive rows already exist, but the default shipped execution flow does not generate the archive shape those stories were designed around.\"],\"architectureFindings\":[\"`ExecutionResult` is still typed as `processHistoryItems: ProcessHistoryItem[]`, and `ProcessHistoryItem` still exposes the legacy presentation vocabulary rather than the canonical archive taxonomy.\",\"The design contract said archive rows would store nullable artifact/source/tool IDs and read services would enrich later; current checkpoint/provenance interfaces do not return the identifiers needed to realize that contract on the live path.\",\"The process work-surface contract/UI never added the designed archive entry point, so archive/turn/view routes are not connected to the primary process surface.\"],\"epicCoverageAssessment\":[\"`corepack pnpm run green-verify` and `corepack pnpm run verify-all` both exited 0.\",\"Automation is masking the main integration gaps: tests such as `tests/service/server/turn-derivation.test.ts` and `tests/service/server/derived-archive-view.test.ts` seed canonical archive rows directly, and `tests/service/server/archive-api.test.ts` seeds provenance-linked rows directly, instead of proving the live runtime can emit them.\",\"The gate is still lighter than the epic implies: `guard:no-test-changes` prints `SKIP` and `test:e2e` is scaffold-only, so there is no executable end-to-end check for live archive generation or archive navigation.\"],\"productionPathFindings\":[\"`createApp` wires `new ScriptExecutionService(providerAdapterRegistry)` by default, and that service still uses the documented Epic 3 default placeholder payload; the placeholder emits a synthetic `process_event` plus \\\"Execution placeholder...\\\" side-work output rather than real low-level archive material.\",\"No production archive append path populates `relatedArtifactVersionId`, `relatedSourceProvenanceId`, or `relatedToolCallId`; the live appenders explicitly write those fields as `null`, so provenance and tool-correlation behavior is unreachable from real traffic.\",\"Checkpoint persistence and source-provenance recording happen only after archive finalization and expose no archive-linkable identifiers back to the archive writer, so Story 6 enrichment currently works only for pre-seeded/test-fixture rows.\"],\"blockingFindings\":[{\"id\":\"EV-E7-001\",\"severity\":\"critical\",\"title\":\"Live execution cannot emit the Epic 7 archive taxonomy\",\"evidence\":\"`ProcessHistoryItem` only allows `user_message|process_message|progress_update|attention_request|side_work_update|process_event` in `apps/platform/shared/contracts/process-work-surface.ts:124-131`, and `ExecutionResult` still exposes `processHistoryItems: ProcessHistoryItem[]` in `apps/platform/server/services/processes/environment/provider-adapter.ts:125-132`. `ProcessHistoryCompatService` only maps `user_message`, `process_message`, and `process_event` into archive kinds in `apps/platform/server/services/archive/process-history-compat.service.ts:8-23`. On the shipped path, `createApp` defaults to `new ScriptExecutionService(providerAdapterRegistry)` in `apps/platform/server/app.ts:285-286`, and that default service still uses the documented Epic 3 placeholder payload in `apps/platform/server/services/processes/environment/script-execution.service.ts:159-177`, which emits only a synthetic `process_event` in `script-execution.service.ts:85-128`. As a result, the runtime cannot produce `reasoning`, `script_emission`, `tool_call`, or `tool_result` archive entries at all, and does not produce real `model_message` traffic without a non-default injected runner.\",\"affectedFiles\":[\"apps/platform/shared/contracts/process-work-surface.ts\",\"apps/platform/server/services/processes/environment/provider-adapter.ts\",\"apps/platform/server/services/archive/process-history-compat.service.ts\",\"apps/platform/server/services/processes/environment/script-execution.service.ts\",\"apps/platform/server/app.ts\"],\"requirementIds\":[\"AC-1.1\",\"AC-1.2\",\"AC-2.3\"],\"recommendedFixScope\":\"fresh-fix-path\",\"blocking\":true},{\"id\":\"EV-E7-002\",\"severity\":\"major\",\"title\":\"Archive rows never capture artifact/source provenance on the live path\",\"evidence\":\"Both live archive appenders hardcode relation fields to `null`: `apps/platform/server/services/archive/process-history-compat.service.ts:39-56` and `apps/platform/server/services/processes/process-response.service.ts:151-167`. During execution, archive finalization happens before provenance recording in `apps/platform/server/services/processes/environment/process-environment.service.ts:563-581` and `690-706`; later checkpoint/provenance steps run separately in `process-environment.service.ts:829-882`. Those downstream interfaces do not return linkable identifiers: `persistCheckpointArtifacts` returns only `PlatformProcessOutputSummary[]` in `apps/platform/server/services/projects/platform-store.ts:386-389`, and `SourceProvenanceService.recordInformedWorkForCurrentSources` / `recordReceivedCodeUpdates` both return `Promise<void>` in `apps/platform/server/services/sources/source-provenance.service.ts:22-34`. The read-time enrichment added for Story 6 therefore depends on IDs that production never writes.\",\"affectedFiles\":[\"apps/platform/server/services/archive/process-history-compat.service.ts\",\"apps/platform/server/services/processes/process-response.service.ts\",\"apps/platform/server/services/processes/environment/process-environment.service.ts\",\"apps/platform/server/services/projects/platform-store.ts\",\"apps/platform/server/services/sources/source-provenance.service.ts\"],\"requirementIds\":[\"AC-1.4\",\"AC-6.1\",\"AC-6.2\",\"AC-6.3\"],\"recommendedFixScope\":\"fresh-fix-path\",\"blocking\":true}],\"nonBlockingFindings\":[{\"id\":\"EV-E7-003\",\"severity\":\"minor\",\"title\":\"Process work surface never exposes an archive entry point\",\"evidence\":\"`renderProcessWorkSurfacePage` accepts callbacks for project, review, start, resume, rehydrate, rebuild, and respond only in `apps/platform/client/features/processes/process-work-surface-page.ts:27-45`, and its control switch has no archive navigation case in `process-work-surface-page.ts:140-169`. The shared control contract likewise only defines `start`, `respond`, `resume`, `rehydrate`, `rebuild`, `review`, and `restart` in `apps/platform/shared/contracts/process-work-surface.ts:176-206`. The archive route exists, but it is not discoverable from the primary process surface.\",\"affectedFiles\":[\"apps/platform/client/features/processes/process-work-surface-page.ts\",\"apps/platform/shared/contracts/process-work-surface.ts\"],\"requirementIds\":[\"BROWSER-ROUTE-CONTRACT\"],\"recommendedFixScope\":\"quick-fix\",\"blocking\":false}],\"unresolvedItems\":[\"`verify-all` passed, but `test:e2e` is scaffold-only and `guard:no-test-changes` is not implemented, so those gate layers remain unproven.\",\"This review did not manually run `pnpm run convex:dev` and `pnpm dev` to validate archive generation against a live backend/provider session.\"],\"gateResult\":\"pass\"},{\"resultId\":\"b4ca1d64-d1f4-434e-a365-46beb9748d92\",\"outcome\":\"block\",\"provider\":\"codex\",\"model\":\"gpt-5.4\",\"reviewerLabel\":\"epic-verifier-2\",\"crossStoryFindings\":[\"The route, store, client, and test surfaces for archive/turn/view reads are wired end to end, and both `corepack pnpm run green-verify` and `corepack pnpm run verify-all` passed.\",\"Cross-story drift remains between the Story 1/2 write path and the Story 4/5/6 read path: turns, derived views, and provenance enrichment assume a richer canonical archive than the shipped execution path actually produces.\",\"Most low-level archive taxonomy and provenance scenarios are proven with fixtures/in-memory stores rather than by the real execution pipeline.\"],\"architectureFindings\":[\"The tech design says Fastify should finalize completed model/runtime objects, script emissions, and tool call/result pairs into canonical archive entries, but the implementation still canonicalizes runtime output through presentation-level `processHistoryItems` compatibility mapping.\",\"The design says `archiveTurns` are cached projections for bounded reads, but turn and derived-view GETs rebuild from full archive scans on each request instead of serving cached projections first.\",\"The design expects archive entries to carry nullable artifact/source/tool foreign keys for read-time enrichment, but the shipped writers persist provenance on parallel tables without linking those ids back onto archive rows.\"],\"epicCoverageAssessment\":[\"Story 3-5 read surfaces are present and exercised by tests, including access control, empty states, degraded rendering, and derived-view conflict handling.\",\"Story 1-2 are only partially realized on the production path: canonical append currently reaches `user_message`, `model_message`, and `process_event`, not the full seven-kind archive taxonomy required by the epic.\",\"Story 6 provenance coherence is implemented as a read-time enrichment layer, but the write path never supplies the archive-side ids that would let real archive entries surface artifact/source provenance.\"],\"productionPathFindings\":[\"The default execution path still runs the explicit placeholder script payload in `apps/platform/server/services/processes/environment/script-execution.service.ts`, and that payload emits a single finalized `process_event` instead of real low-level reasoning/script/tool archive objects.\",\"Artifact checkpoints and source-provenance records are persisted on side channels, but the shipped archive writers never attach `relatedArtifactVersionId` or `relatedSourceProvenanceId` to canonical archive entries.\",\"Archive source-provenance enrichment only looks at the newest 200 provenance rows for a process, so older archive pages can report healthy links as degraded once real archive rows start linking to older provenance ids.\",\"Turn and derived-view reads currently pay full-archive rebuild cost on every request rather than using cached projections as the primary bounded read path.\"],\"blockingFindings\":[{\"id\":\"EV-07-001\",\"severity\":\"critical\",\"title\":\"The shipped archive write path never produces four of the seven required canonical entry kinds\",\"evidence\":\"`ExecutionResult` only carries `processHistoryItems`, outputs, side-work writes, and checkpoint candidates (`apps/platform/server/services/processes/environment/provider-adapter.ts:125-132`). `processHistoryItemKindSchema` is limited to `user_message`, `process_message`, `progress_update`, `attention_request`, `side_work_update`, and `process_event` (`apps/platform/shared/contracts/process-work-surface.ts:124-131`). Runtime execution stores those history items and then archives them through `appendFromProcessHistoryItem` (`apps/platform/server/services/processes/environment/process-environment.service.ts:690-706`), while `ProcessHistoryCompatService` only maps `user_message`, `process_message`, and `process_event` into archive entries and hard-codes the related ids to `null` (`apps/platform/server/services/archive/process-history-compat.service.ts:8-12`, `:39-56`). The default production script payload is still the shared placeholder and only emits a finalized `process_event` (`apps/platform/server/services/processes/environment/script-execution.service.ts:15-135`, `:158-163`). As shipped, the real path never emits `reasoning`, `script_emission`, `tool_call`, or `tool_result` archive entries.\",\"affectedFiles\":[\"apps/platform/server/services/processes/environment/provider-adapter.ts\",\"apps/platform/shared/contracts/process-work-surface.ts\",\"apps/platform/server/services/processes/environment/process-environment.service.ts\",\"apps/platform/server/services/archive/process-history-compat.service.ts\",\"apps/platform/server/services/processes/environment/script-execution.service.ts\"],\"requirementIds\":[\"AC-1.1\",\"AC-1.2\",\"AC-2.3\",\"AC-4.1\"],\"recommendedFixScope\":\"fresh-fix-path\",\"blocking\":true},{\"id\":\"EV-07-002\",\"severity\":\"major\",\"title\":\"Archive provenance coherence is unreachable on the real write path because archive rows never record related artifact/source ids\",\"evidence\":\"Accepted user-response archiving explicitly writes `relatedArtifactVersionId: null` and `relatedSourceProvenanceId: null` (`apps/platform/server/services/processes/process-response.service.ts:151-167`). The compatibility archive path also hard-codes all related ids to `null` (`apps/platform/server/services/archive/process-history-compat.service.ts:39-56`). Meanwhile the execution/checkpoint flow persists artifacts and source provenance on separate paths via `persistCheckpointArtifacts`, `recordInformedWorkForCurrentSources`, and `recordReceivedCodeUpdates` (`apps/platform/server/services/processes/environment/process-environment.service.ts:577-581`, `:830-883`), and `SourceProvenanceService` creates durable provenance rows separately (`apps/platform/server/services/sources/source-provenance.service.ts:200-218`). Because no shipped archive writer threads those ids back onto archive entries, the Story 6 enrichment surface is only reachable from fixtures/tests, not from real archive data.\",\"affectedFiles\":[\"apps/platform/server/services/processes/process-response.service.ts\",\"apps/platform/server/services/archive/process-history-compat.service.ts\",\"apps/platform/server/services/processes/environment/process-environment.service.ts\",\"apps/platform/server/services/sources/source-provenance.service.ts\"],\"requirementIds\":[\"AC-1.4\",\"AC-6.1\",\"AC-6.2\"],\"recommendedFixScope\":\"fresh-fix-path\",\"blocking\":true}],\"nonBlockingFindings\":[{\"id\":\"EV-07-003\",\"severity\":\"major\",\"title\":\"Source provenance enrichment can falsely degrade older archive entries because it only loads the newest 200 provenance rows\",\"evidence\":\"`listProcessSourceProvenanceEntries` returns only the 200 most recent source-provenance records for a process (`convex/sourceProvenance.ts:58-71`). `ArchiveReadService` loads that process-wide slice once when any page contains `relatedSourceProvenanceId` values (`apps/platform/server/services/archive/archive-read.service.ts:120-126`) and resolves each entry from that in-memory map (`apps/platform/server/services/archive/archive-read.service.ts:148-160`). If an archive page references an older but still-existing provenance id outside the newest 200 rows, the entry is incorrectly degraded with `Related source provenance is unavailable.` (`apps/platform/server/services/archive/archive-read.service.ts:198-200`).\",\"affectedFiles\":[\"convex/sourceProvenance.ts\",\"apps/platform/server/services/archive/archive-read.service.ts\"],\"requirementIds\":[\"AC-3.4\",\"AC-6.2\",\"AC-6.3\"],\"recommendedFixScope\":\"quick-fix\",\"blocking\":false},{\"id\":\"EV-07-004\",\"severity\":\"major\",\"title\":\"Turn and derived-view reads bypass the cached-projection design and rescan the full archive on every request\",\"evidence\":\"`getTurns` always calls `rebuildTurns` before reading a page (`apps/platform/server/services/archive/turn-derivation.service.ts:61-85`), and `rebuildTurns` paginates through the entire archive (`apps/platform/server/services/archive/turn-derivation.service.ts:89-110`). `listViews` and `refreshViews` likewise rebuild turns and recompute full-archive signatures by scanning all archive entries before responding (`apps/platform/server/services/archive/derived-archive-view.service.ts:50-86`, `:100-143`, `:148-182`). Functionally this works, but it drifts from the tech design's cached/bounded projection model for long-running processes.\",\"affectedFiles\":[\"apps/platform/server/services/archive/turn-derivation.service.ts\",\"apps/platform/server/services/archive/derived-archive-view.service.ts\"],\"requirementIds\":[\"AC-4.1\",\"AC-7.1\"],\"recommendedFixScope\":\"fresh-fix-path\",\"blocking\":false}],\"unresolvedItems\":[\"The 2-second performance NFR for turn/archive reads at 5,000 archive entries was not measured against a real Convex-backed runtime during this review.\",\"Manual end-to-end verification with `pnpm run convex:dev` and `pnpm dev` was not performed; production-path conclusions are based on code inspection plus automated test results.\"],\"gateResult\":\"pass\"}]},\"errors\":[],\"warnings\":[],\"artifacts\":[{\"kind\":\"result-envelope\",\"path\":\"/Users/leemoore/code/liminal-build/docs/spec-build/v2/epics/07--archive-and-derived-views/artifacts/epic/002-epic-verifier-batch.json\"}],\"startedAt\":\"2026-05-05T09:15:32.432Z\",\"finishedAt\":\"2026-05-05T09:25:20.895Z\"}\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/07--archive-and-derived-views/artifacts/epic/005-epic-verifier-batch.json:1:{\"command\":\"epic-verify\",\"version\":1,\"status\":\"blocked\",\"outcome\":\"block\",\"result\":{\"outcome\":\"block\",\"verifierResults\":[{\"resultId\":\"c143b247-c13b-48cd-ac42-7cf34522e355\",\"outcome\":\"block\",\"provider\":\"codex\",\"model\":\"gpt-5.4\",\"reviewerLabel\":\"epic-verifier-1\",\"crossStoryFindings\":[\"The derived-view pagination change is only partially propagated: shared contracts, route/schema wiring, the derived-view service, PlatformStore implementations, and several test doubles no longer agree on the `listDerivedArchiveViews` request/response shape.\",\"Turn and derived-view cache behavior now diverges between the in-memory test store and the Convex production store, so cross-story reopen behavior is not being validated against the real persistence path.\",\"Archive capture, turn derivation, and derived-view surfaces are conceptually aligned around archive truth, but the default execution path that feeds the archive is still a canned runtime-audit script rather than real process-specific execution.\"],\"architectureFindings\":[\"The tech design says turn and derived-view rebuilds happen on read from canonical archive data; the current services only rebuild when the cached first page is empty, which is weaker than the documented contract.\",\"The architecture expects Fastify pagination contracts to match store and durable-layer contracts end to end; the current derived-view rollout breaks that consistency and fails the type gate before tests can run.\",\"Canonical archive truth is supposed to preserve finalized process work, but the default production executor still synthesizes archive entries from a hard-coded audit payload.\"],\"epicCoverageAssessment\":[\"`corepack pnpm run verify-all` fails in `typecheck`, so none of the Epic 7 service, client, integration, or e2e tests actually execute to green.\",\"The added Story 6/7 tests around detached-source degradation and bounded derived-view pages improve intended coverage, but they currently provide no passing evidence because the build is broken first.\",\"Static inspection found a production-only stale-cache path that the in-memory tests mask, so even a later green test run should explicitly verify Convex-backed reopen/read behavior.\"],\"productionPathFindings\":[\"The production app wires `new ScriptExecutionService(providerAdapterRegistry)` by default, and that service's default payload factory emits a synthetic integrated runtime-audit script that fabricates `reasoning`, `tool_call`, `tool_result`, `model_message`, `process_event`, and `script_emission` archive entries.\",\"`InMemoryPlatformStore` deletes cached turns and derived views on archive append/patch, but `ConvexPlatformStore` does not, so production can serve stale derived data even though the primary test store self-heals.\",\"No equivalent fake adapter was found in the archive read routes themselves; the material non-real execution paths are the canned script executor and the test-only cache invalidation behavior.\"],\"blockingFindings\":[{\"id\":\"EPIC7-DERIVED-VIEW-PAGINATION-ROLLUP\",\"severity\":\"critical\",\"title\":\"Derived-view pagination refactor is incomplete and breaks the epic gate\",\"evidence\":\"Running `corepack pnpm run verify-all` fails in `typecheck` before any Epic 7 tests run. The current rollout leaves `DefaultDerivedArchiveViewService` and multiple store/test implementations disagreeing about the `listDerivedArchiveViews` shape: TypeScript reports `'cursor' does not exist in type '{ processId: string; }'`, `'views' does not exist on type 'DerivedArchiveView[]'`, plus contract failures in `tests/service/server/processes-api.test.ts`, `tests/service/server/auth-routes.test.ts`, and `tests/service/server/derived-archive-view.test.ts`.\",\"affectedFiles\":[\"apps/platform/server/services/archive/derived-archive-view.service.ts\",\"apps/platform/server/services/projects/platform-store.ts\",\"apps/platform/shared/contracts/archive.ts\",\"tests/service/server/processes-api.test.ts\",\"tests/service/server/auth-routes.test.ts\"],\"requirementIds\":[\"AC-5.1\",\"AC-7.1\",\"AC-7.3\"],\"recommendedFixScope\":\"same-session-implementor\",\"blocking\":true},{\"id\":\"EPIC7-STale-DERIVED-CACHE-PRODUCTION\",\"severity\":\"major\",\"title\":\"Convex production reads can return stale turns and derived views after new archive entries arrive\",\"evidence\":\"`DefaultTurnDerivationService.getTurns` rebuilds only when the first cached page is empty, and `DefaultDerivedArchiveViewService.listViews` now does the same. In production, `ConvexPlatformStore.appendArchiveEntry` and `patchArchiveEntry` only write archive rows; they never clear `archiveTurns` or `derivedArchiveViews`. By contrast, `InMemoryPlatformStore` explicitly deletes those caches on append/patch and after turn upserts. After the first successful rebuild, later archive appends in Convex can leave `/archive/turns` and `/archive/derived-views` stale indefinitely until an explicit refresh.\",\"affectedFiles\":[\"apps/platform/server/services/archive/turn-derivation.service.ts\",\"apps/platform/server/services/archive/derived-archive-view.service.ts\",\"apps/platform/server/services/projects/platform-store.ts\"],\"requirementIds\":[\"AC-4.1\",\"AC-5.1\",\"AC-7.1\"],\"recommendedFixScope\":\"fresh-fix-path\",\"blocking\":true},{\"id\":\"EPIC7-SYNTHETIC-ARCHIVE-PRODUCTION-PATH\",\"severity\":\"major\",\"title\":\"The default production archive capture path still archives a canned runtime-audit script, not real process execution\",\"evidence\":\"`apps/platform/server/app.ts` constructs `new ScriptExecutionService(providerAdapterRegistry)` when no override is injected. The default `ScriptExecutionService` payload factory always returns `buildIntegratedRuntimeAuditPayload`, whose hard-coded TypeScript module writes a runtime report and emits synthetic archive entries for `reasoning`, `tool_call`, `tool_result`, `model_message`, `process_event`, and `script_emission`. That means the live production path feeding Epic 7 is still a placeholder execution program rather than real process-specific work.\",\"affectedFiles\":[\"apps/platform/server/app.ts\",\"apps/platform/server/services/processes/environment/script-execution.service.ts\",\"apps/platform/server/services/processes/environment/process-environment.service.ts\"],\"requirementIds\":[\"AC-1.1\",\"AC-2.3\"],\"recommendedFixScope\":\"human-ruling\",\"blocking\":true}],\"nonBlockingFindings\":[],\"unresolvedItems\":[\"Rerun `corepack pnpm run green-verify` and `corepack pnpm run verify-all` after finishing the derived-view pagination rollout; the current review could not observe any post-typecheck test results.\",\"Decide whether the integrated runtime-audit payload is an accepted temporary production path or a release blocker for Epic 7 shipping.\",\"After fixing the cache policy, verify turn and derived-view reopen behavior against the real Convex store, not only `InMemoryPlatformStore`.\"],\"gateResult\":\"fail\"},{\"resultId\":\"fc533748-7b73-42a8-9606-55f12e2f4677\",\"outcome\":\"block\",\"provider\":\"codex\",\"model\":\"gpt-5.4\",\"reviewerLabel\":\"epic-verifier-2\",\"crossStoryFindings\":[\"Archive entry reads and turn derivation are mostly intact, but the derived-view slice is currently broken: `tests/service/server/archive-api.test.ts` passed 15/15 and `tests/service/server/turn-derivation.test.ts` passed 8/8, while `tests/service/server/derived-archive-view.test.ts` now fails 6 of 7 cases with 500s.\",\"The archive/turn/view layers no longer react consistently to provenance-only degradation. `/archive` re-enriches entries per read, but cached turns/views can stay stale after source detachment or related-context loss.\"],\"architectureFindings\":[\"A partial derived-view pagination refactor drifted across layers. `DefaultDerivedArchiveViewService` expects paged stored-view reads, but lower store/Convex seams and several callers still assume the older array-returning contract.\",\"Derived projections are only invalidated on archive writes. Source/artifact state changes do not invalidate or recompute `archiveTurns` / derived views, so the rebuildable-projection contract no longer matches the archive read path's degraded-state behavior.\"],\"epicCoverageAssessment\":[\"Archive append/read, access checks, and turn derivation still have meaningful coverage: `archive-api.test.ts` passed 15/15 and `turn-derivation.test.ts` passed 8/8 when run directly.\",\"Derived-view coverage is red. `derived-archive-view.test.ts` fails TC-5.1a, TC-5.2a/5.3a/5.3b, the degraded-on-reopen scenario, TC-7.1b, bounded paging, and the derived-view cache invalidation scenario.\",\"Epic 7 is not green end-to-end because Story 5/7 behavior is down and the turn/view degraded-state contract is inconsistent with Story 6 provenance degradation.\"],\"productionPathFindings\":[\"The live derived-view read path is materially broken right now. `corepack pnpm vitest run tests/service/server/derived-archive-view.test.ts` returns 500s for the GET `/archive/derived-views` scenarios, so the structural-view surface is not usable.\",\"Turn and derived-view caches are not refreshed when only related provenance changes. A source detachment can change `/archive` output immediately while `/archive/turns` and cached derived views keep serving pre-detachment readiness.\"],\"blockingFindings\":[{\"id\":\"EV-07-01\",\"severity\":\"major\",\"title\":\"Derived-view read path is broken by a partially applied pagination contract change\",\"evidence\":\"`corepack pnpm run typecheck` reports `apps/platform/server/services/archive/derived-archive-view.service.ts(254,48)` because `listAllStoredViews` is still calling `platformStore.listDerivedArchiveViews({ processId })` while the new signature requires paging, and `tests/service/server/derived-archive-view.test.ts(417,61)` / `tests/service/server/processes-api.test.ts(341,5)` show callers still returning arrays instead of `{ views, page }`. Running `corepack pnpm vitest run tests/service/server/derived-archive-view.test.ts` now yields 6 failing 500s, and `corepack pnpm vitest run convex/archiveEntries.test.ts` still fails the derived-view primitive expectations.\",\"affectedFiles\":[\"apps/platform/server/services/archive/derived-archive-view.service.ts\",\"apps/platform/server/services/projects/platform-store.ts\",\"convex/derivedArchiveViews.ts\",\"tests/service/server/derived-archive-view.test.ts\",\"tests/service/server/processes-api.test.ts\",\"convex/archiveEntries.test.ts\"],\"requirementIds\":[\"AC-5.1\",\"AC-5.2\",\"AC-5.3\",\"AC-5.5\",\"AC-7.1\",\"AC-7.3\"],\"recommendedFixScope\":\"same-session-implementor\",\"blocking\":true},{\"id\":\"EV-07-02\",\"severity\":\"major\",\"title\":\"Cached turns and derived views do not re-derive when provenance degrades after the archive is written\",\"evidence\":\"`DefaultArchiveReadService` re-enriches archive entries on every read (`apps/platform/server/services/archive/archive-read.service.ts:52-65` plus `apps/platform/server/services/archive/archive-entry-enrichment.ts:10-152`), but `DefaultTurnDerivationService.getTurns` only rebuilds when the cached turn page is empty (`apps/platform/server/services/archive/turn-derivation.service.ts:87-98`). I reproduced this by building turns, detaching the linked source attachment, and calling `getTurns` again; the second response still returned the original `ready` turn. The derived-view service follows the same cache-first pattern, so reopen behavior can diverge between `/archive`, `/archive/turns`, and cached derived views after source detachment or provenance degradation.\",\"affectedFiles\":[\"apps/platform/server/services/archive/archive-read.service.ts\",\"apps/platform/server/services/archive/archive-entry-enrichment.ts\",\"apps/platform/server/services/archive/turn-derivation.service.ts\",\"apps/platform/server/services/archive/derived-archive-view.service.ts\"],\"requirementIds\":[\"AC-4.4\",\"AC-6.3\",\"AC-7.1\"],\"recommendedFixScope\":\"fresh-fix-path\",\"blocking\":true}],\"nonBlockingFindings\":[],\"unresolvedItems\":[\"Both named gates are failed, but neither completed a clean full sweep: `corepack pnpm run green-verify` and `corepack pnpm run verify-all` stopped immediately in `format:check` on `convex/derivedArchiveViews.ts`, so the remaining lint/build/integration stages were not reached in a passing run.\",\"The provenance-staleness regression was reproduced manually at the service layer; there is no current automated regression test covering cache refresh after source detachment.\"],\"gateResult\":\"fail\"}]},\"errors\":[],\"warnings\":[],\"artifacts\":[{\"kind\":\"result-envelope\",\"path\":\"/Users/leemoore/code/liminal-build/docs/spec-build/v2/epics/07--archive-and-derived-views/artifacts/epic/005-epic-verifier-batch.json\"}],\"startedAt\":\"2026-05-05T11:29:07.087Z\",\"finishedAt\":\"2026-05-05T11:48:15.053Z\"}\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/07--archive-and-derived-views/artifacts/epic/003-epic-verifier-batch.json:1:{\"command\":\"epic-verify\",\"version\":1,\"status\":\"blocked\",\"outcome\":\"block\",\"result\":{\"outcome\":\"block\",\"verifierResults\":[{\"resultId\":\"67138ffb-df0f-4ac8-8ea2-ae7ae3d35994\",\"outcome\":\"block\",\"provider\":\"codex\",\"model\":\"gpt-5.4\",\"reviewerLabel\":\"epic-verifier-1\",\"crossStoryFindings\":[\"Stories 1-7 are wired end-to-end through shared contracts, Convex tables, Fastify routes, and client archive surfaces, and both requested verification gates succeeded.\",\"The cross-story happy path works, but the execution-to-archive handoff still breaks canonical-truth guarantees in two places: production runs emit placeholder archive content, and deferred entries are dropped instead of downgraded when provenance/checkpoint resolution fails.\"],\"architectureFindings\":[\"The archive storage/read architecture is coherent, but the execution boundary drifts from the tech design: `createApp` composes a real provider registry while `ScriptExecutionService` still defaults to a canned payload instead of a process-specific runtime.\",\"Turn and derived-view GET reads rebuild projections on every request rather than primarily serving cached projections, which weakens the bounded-read strategy described in the tech design for long histories.\"],\"epicCoverageAssessment\":[\"Implemented coverage is strong on the green path: archive persistence, archive APIs, turn derivation, derived-view responses, and provenance enrichment all shipped and `corepack pnpm run green-verify` plus `corepack pnpm run verify-all` both succeeded.\",\"Coverage is incomplete on degraded production behavior: there is no protection against losing deferred canonical entries when artifact/source linkage cannot be resolved at append time.\",\"The epic gate passed, but the `test:e2e` leg is still scaffold-only, so no executable browser/runtime end-to-end archive scenario is currently enforced by automation.\"],\"productionPathFindings\":[\"The in-memory/failing provider adapters and stub checkpoint writer are clearly test-only seams and are not the material concern.\",\"The material non-real production path is `ScriptExecutionService`'s default payload, which fabricates a `Default Execution Summary`, canned reasoning/tool/model/process archive entries, and a dummy source checkpoint note for writable repos.\",\"When deferred archive entries depend on artifact or source provenance, the production orchestrator currently skips the entry entirely if that relation cannot be resolved, creating a missing-history path instead of a degraded-but-readable canonical archive record.\"],\"blockingFindings\":[{\"id\":\"EV-ARCHIVE-001\",\"severity\":\"critical\",\"title\":\"Production executions still archive placeholder output instead of real process work\",\"evidence\":\"The production composition root instantiates `new ScriptExecutionService(providerAdapterRegistry)` with no custom payload factory (`apps/platform/server/app.ts:285-286`), so runtime execution falls back to `buildDefaultScriptPayload`. That default script writes a `Default Execution Summary`, emits canned `reasoning`, `tool_call`, `tool_result`, `model_message`, `process_event`, and `script_emission` archive entries, and stages a dummy writable-source file with commit message `Record default execution note` (`apps/platform/server/services/processes/environment/script-execution.service.ts:15-317`).\",\"affectedFiles\":[\"apps/platform/server/app.ts\",\"apps/platform/server/services/processes/environment/script-execution.service.ts\"],\"requirementIds\":[\"AC-1.1\",\"AC-2.3\"],\"recommendedFixScope\":\"fresh-fix-path\",\"blocking\":true},{\"id\":\"EV-ARCHIVE-002\",\"severity\":\"major\",\"title\":\"Deferred archive entries are silently dropped when provenance or checkpoint relations cannot be resolved\",\"evidence\":\"The orchestrator defers entries with `artifactCheckpointIndex` or `sourceProvenanceBinding`, but `appendDeferredArchiveEntries` uses `continue` when the related artifact version or source provenance record is missing (`apps/platform/server/services/processes/environment/process-environment.service.ts:783-810`). A direct repro against that helper returned `{\\\"entries\\\":[],\\\"page\\\":{\\\"cursor\\\":null,\\\"nextCursor\\\":null,\\\"hasMore\\\":false}}` after attempting to append a deferred `script_emission` entry with unresolved relations, so canonical history is lost instead of surfaced as degraded metadata.\",\"affectedFiles\":[\"apps/platform/server/services/processes/environment/process-environment.service.ts\"],\"requirementIds\":[\"AC-1.4\",\"AC-6.3\",\"AC-7.2\"],\"recommendedFixScope\":\"quick-fix\",\"blocking\":true}],\"nonBlockingFindings\":[{\"id\":\"EV-ARCHIVE-003\",\"severity\":\"observation\",\"title\":\"Turn and derived-view reads bypass the intended cache-first bounded-read design\",\"evidence\":\"Every `GET /archive/turns` request forces `rebuildTurns` before listing turns (`apps/platform/server/services/archive/turn-derivation.service.ts:61-85`), and `GET /archive/derived-views` likewise rebuilds turns and rewrites stored views on read (`apps/platform/server/services/archive/derived-archive-view.service.ts:50-75`). This preserves correctness today but adds avoidable full-archive work and write amplification on normal reads.\",\"affectedFiles\":[\"apps/platform/server/services/archive/turn-derivation.service.ts\",\"apps/platform/server/services/archive/derived-archive-view.service.ts\"],\"requirementIds\":[\"AC-7.1\",\"AC-7.3\"],\"recommendedFixScope\":\"fresh-fix-path\",\"blocking\":false}],\"unresolvedItems\":[\"Decide whether the placeholder execution payload is an explicit temporary stopgap or an unintended leftover from Epic 3; either way it should not ship as canonical archive truth.\",\"No executable e2e suite currently verifies the browser/runtime archive flow because `test:e2e` is scaffold-only.\"],\"gateResult\":\"pass\"},{\"resultId\":\"7e8e159e-b398-4820-ad73-1e4ceb24971c\",\"outcome\":\"block\",\"provider\":\"codex\",\"model\":\"gpt-5.4\",\"reviewerLabel\":\"epic-verifier-2\",\"crossStoryFindings\":[\"Canonical archive append/read, turn derivation, derived-view routes, and client surfaces are implemented end to end, and both `green-verify` and `verify-all` passed.\",\"The degraded-state story is inconsistent across surfaces: archive-entry degradation is computed in the archive read service, but turn and derived-view rebuilds read raw archive rows and can report the same process slice as `ready`.\",\"The deferred finalization path is not lossless. Under partial artifact/provenance failure it can drop finalized entries entirely, which breaks reopen consistency and any later turn/view derivation that depends on the archive as canonical truth.\"],\"architectureFindings\":[\"`ArchiveReadService` bypasses the existing source-provenance read service and rehydrates source provenance from raw store rows, so archive-source coherence can drift from the rest of the source domain.\",\"Flow 7 in the tech design says archive, turns, and derived views use cursor-bounded reads; derived views currently implement only a hard `slice(0, 50)` with no cursor/query contract.\",\"The production runtime still exercises archive finalization through the shared default placeholder script payload rather than process-type-specific execution logic.\"],\"epicCoverageAssessment\":[\"Happy-path coverage is strong: durable archive tables, archive routes, turn rebuilds, structural derived views, provenance enrichment, and client rendering are all present and exercised by passing tests.\",\"Coverage is weak for degraded reopen scenarios. The existing suites assert missing-record degradation on archive reads, but they do not catch deferred-entry loss, turn/view degradation drift, or source-detach/access-revocation behavior after reopen.\",\"Epic 7 is close on the happy path, but the current implementation does not fully preserve the 'archive stays visible and projections degrade locally' contract under partial-failure conditions.\"],\"productionPathFindings\":[\"I did not find the in-memory provider fake wired into production; the material non-real path is the real runtime default in `ScriptExecutionService`, which still emits a canned 'default execution payload'.\",\"`appendDeferredArchiveEntries` has a lossy production branch: unresolved artifact/source bindings cause the code to skip the finalized entry instead of persisting a degraded canonical row.\"],\"blockingFindings\":[{\"id\":\"EV-001\",\"severity\":\"critical\",\"title\":\"Deferred archive entries are silently dropped when related artifact or source provenance cannot be resolved\",\"evidence\":\"`appendDeferredArchiveEntries` resolves `artifactCheckpointIndex` / `sourceProvenanceBinding` and then `continue`s when either lookup is missing (`apps/platform/server/services/processes/environment/process-environment.service.ts` lines 783-810). That drops finalized deferred entries instead of appending a degraded archive row, violating the archive-truth requirement when checkpoint/provenance side effects partially fail.\",\"affectedFiles\":[\"apps/platform/server/services/processes/environment/process-environment.service.ts\"],\"requirementIds\":[\"AC-1.4\",\"AC-6.3\",\"AC-7.1\"],\"recommendedFixScope\":\"same-session-implementor\",\"blocking\":true},{\"id\":\"EV-002\",\"severity\":\"major\",\"title\":\"Turn and derived-view rebuilds ignore related-context degradation computed by archive reads\",\"evidence\":\"`TurnDerivationService.rebuildTurns` pages raw archive rows from `platformStore.listArchiveEntries` (`apps/platform/server/services/archive/turn-derivation.service.ts` lines 48-50 and 89-111) and only degrades turns when the stored row already has `entryStatus === 'degraded'` (lines 149-154). Missing artifact/source context is added later by `ArchiveReadService` (`apps/platform/server/services/archive/archive-read.service.ts` lines 163-224), so turns and derived views can stay `ready` while the archive page shows degraded entries.\",\"affectedFiles\":[\"apps/platform/server/services/archive/turn-derivation.service.ts\",\"apps/platform/server/services/archive/derived-archive-view.service.ts\",\"apps/platform/server/services/archive/archive-read.service.ts\"],\"requirementIds\":[\"AC-4.4\",\"AC-5.5\",\"AC-7.2\"],\"recommendedFixScope\":\"fresh-fix-path\",\"blocking\":true},{\"id\":\"EV-003\",\"severity\":\"major\",\"title\":\"Archive reopen bypasses source-provenance degradation logic for detached or revoked sources\",\"evidence\":\"`ArchiveReadService` loads raw `StoredSourceProvenanceRecord` rows and copies their stored `entryStatus` / `degradationReason` directly into archive responses (`apps/platform/server/services/archive/archive-read.service.ts` lines 120-125 and 198-212). The actual read-time degradation logic for detached/redacted/unavailable sources lives in `DefaultSourceProvenanceService.listProcessSourceProvenance` / `buildSourceProvenanceEntry` (`apps/platform/server/services/sources/source-provenance.service.ts` lines 153-199 and 223-285). A source that later detaches or loses access will still read as `ready` in the archive.\",\"affectedFiles\":[\"apps/platform/server/services/archive/archive-read.service.ts\",\"apps/platform/server/services/sources/source-provenance.service.ts\"],\"requirementIds\":[\"AC-6.2\",\"AC-6.3\",\"AC-7.1\"],\"recommendedFixScope\":\"fresh-fix-path\",\"blocking\":true}],\"nonBlockingFindings\":[{\"id\":\"EV-004\",\"severity\":\"minor\",\"title\":\"Derived-view reads are bounded but not cursor-paginated as designed\",\"evidence\":\"Flow 7 says archive entries, turns, and derived views use cursor pagination with default limits (`docs/spec-build/v2/epics/07--archive-and-derived-views/tech-design.md` lines 668-674). The derived-view route schema has no querystring contract (`apps/platform/server/schemas/archive.ts` lines 37-46), and the service simply `slice(0, 50)`s the computed set (`apps/platform/server/services/archive/derived-archive-view.service.ts` lines 210-211).\",\"affectedFiles\":[\"apps/platform/server/schemas/archive.ts\",\"apps/platform/server/services/archive/derived-archive-view.service.ts\",\"apps/platform/shared/contracts/archive.ts\"],\"requirementIds\":[\"AC-7.3\"],\"recommendedFixScope\":\"fresh-fix-path\",\"blocking\":false},{\"id\":\"EV-005\",\"severity\":\"major\",\"title\":\"Production execution still runs through a placeholder default script payload\",\"evidence\":\"`ScriptExecutionService` builds a canned 'default execution payload' with fixed artifact/tool/archive output text (`apps/platform/server/services/processes/environment/script-execution.service.ts` lines 15-18 and 52-60), placeholder side-work summaries (`lines 233-236`), and an explicit comment that process-type-specific payloads 'come later' (`lines 279-283`). This is a real runtime default, not just test infrastructure.\",\"affectedFiles\":[\"apps/platform/server/services/processes/environment/script-execution.service.ts\"],\"requirementIds\":[],\"recommendedFixScope\":\"human-ruling\",\"blocking\":false}],\"unresolvedItems\":[\"`green-verify` and `verify-all` both passed, but `guard:no-test-changes` currently prints `SKIP`, so the story gate's extra protection is scaffolded rather than enforced.\",\"Whether the placeholder default execution payload is accepted temporary debt outside Epic 7 needs an explicit product/architecture ruling before treating the archive path as production-real.\"],\"gateResult\":\"pass\"}]},\"errors\":[],\"warnings\":[],\"artifacts\":[{\"kind\":\"result-envelope\",\"path\":\"/Users/leemoore/code/liminal-build/docs/spec-build/v2/epics/07--archive-and-derived-views/artifacts/epic/003-epic-verifier-batch.json\"}],\"startedAt\":\"2026-05-05T09:51:17.378Z\",\"finishedAt\":\"2026-05-05T09:59:52.997Z\"}\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/07--archive-and-derived-views/artifacts/epic/001-epic-verifier-batch.json:1:{\"command\":\"epic-verify\",\"version\":1,\"status\":\"blocked\",\"outcome\":\"block\",\"result\":{\"outcome\":\"block\",\"verifierResults\":[{\"resultId\":\"d30cc7a8-5f82-4f6a-b137-9154cc2be026\",\"outcome\":\"block\",\"provider\":\"codex\",\"model\":\"gpt-5.4\",\"reviewerLabel\":\"epic-verifier-1\",\"crossStoryFindings\":[\"Stories 3-5 are coherent once canonical archive rows already exist: archive reads, turn derivation, and derived views share stable IDs and degradation semantics.\",\"The seam between Story 2 finalization and Story 1 persistence is where the epic breaks: live execution output is still funneled through legacy `processHistoryItems`, so later stories rely on archive row shapes that the shipped runtime cannot actually produce.\",\"Story 6 provenance enrichment and Story 5 tool-aware turn/view behavior are both validated mostly against hand-seeded archive rows rather than rows emitted by the real completion hooks.\"],\"architectureFindings\":[\"The Convex storage layer matches the tech design, but the control-plane finalization boundary never moved up to finalized runtime objects; it is still coupled to presentation-oriented `ProcessHistoryItem` records.\",\"Read-time enrichment is correctly separated from canonical truth, but no upstream writer populates the related artifact/source IDs that the enrichment layer consumes.\",\"Derived turns and derived views remain rebuildable projections and do not mutate archive truth; the main architectural drift is at capture time, not projection time.\"],\"epicCoverageAssessment\":[\"Both requested gates passed on May 5, 2026: `corepack pnpm run green-verify` and `corepack pnpm run verify-all`.\",\"Coverage is strong for storage, ordering, pagination, turn grouping, derived-view refresh, and degraded-read behavior once archive rows already exist.\",\"Coverage is weak on end-to-end emission: tests create `tool_call`, `tool_result`, and provenance-bearing archive rows directly in fixtures/service stores instead of proving that the live runtime can emit them.\",\"`verify-all` still ends with a scaffold-only `test:e2e` step, so no browser-level end-to-end archive flow currently executes.\"],\"productionPathFindings\":[\"The default runtime path is still the shared placeholder execution payload in `apps/platform/server/services/processes/environment/script-execution.service.ts`, and that payload emits a synthetic `process_event` plus placeholder side-work text instead of a real process-type model/tool/runtime flow.\",\"Production archive append is currently limited to accepted user responses and legacy history-item bridging; there is no real append path for `reasoning`, `script_emission`, `tool_call`, or `tool_result` entries.\",\"Artifact/source provenance enrichment is real on read, but no live writer currently persists the related artifact-version or source-provenance IDs that the read path expects.\"],\"blockingFindings\":[{\"id\":\"archive-taxonomy-production-gap\",\"severity\":\"critical\",\"title\":\"The shipped archive pipeline cannot emit four of the seven required canonical entry kinds\",\"evidence\":\"`ExecutionResult` only carries legacy `ProcessHistoryItem[]` (`apps/platform/server/services/processes/environment/provider-adapter.ts`), `processHistoryItemKindSchema` only allows `user_message`, `process_message`, `progress_update`, `attention_request`, `side_work_update`, and `process_event` (`apps/platform/shared/contracts/process-work-surface.ts`), and the archive compatibility bridge maps only `user_message`, `process_message`, and `process_event` into canonical rows (`apps/platform/server/services/archive/process-history-compat.service.ts`). `ProcessEnvironmentService` archives runtime output only through that bridge (`apps/platform/server/services/processes/environment/process-environment.service.ts`), so the live system has no real append path for `reasoning`, `script_emission`, `tool_call`, or `tool_result`.\",\"affectedFiles\":[\"apps/platform/server/services/processes/environment/provider-adapter.ts\",\"apps/platform/shared/contracts/process-work-surface.ts\",\"apps/platform/server/services/archive/process-history-compat.service.ts\",\"apps/platform/server/services/processes/environment/process-environment.service.ts\",\"apps/platform/server/services/processes/process-response.service.ts\"],\"requirementIds\":[\"AC-1.1\",\"AC-1.2\",\"AC-2.3\"],\"recommendedFixScope\":\"fresh-fix-path\",\"blocking\":true},{\"id\":\"archive-provenance-write-gap\",\"severity\":\"major\",\"title\":\"Live archive writes never attach artifact-version or source-provenance references\",\"evidence\":\"The read path is built to enrich `relatedArtifactVersionId` and `relatedSourceProvenanceId` (`apps/platform/server/services/archive/archive-read.service.ts`), but the shipped producers hard-code both fields to `null` (`apps/platform/server/services/processes/process-response.service.ts`, `apps/platform/server/services/archive/process-history-compat.service.ts`). The only execution-bridge payload is `ProcessHistoryItem`, which exposes `relatedArtifactId` but no artifact-version or source-provenance field (`apps/platform/shared/contracts/process-work-surface.ts`), so real archive rows cannot satisfy provenance visibility requirements. The passing provenance tests seed those IDs directly in fixtures and test stores (`tests/service/server/archive-api.test.ts`, `tests/fixtures/archive.ts`) instead of proving a live producer can emit them.\",\"affectedFiles\":[\"apps/platform/server/services/archive/archive-read.service.ts\",\"apps/platform/server/services/processes/process-response.service.ts\",\"apps/platform/server/services/archive/process-history-compat.service.ts\",\"apps/platform/shared/contracts/process-work-surface.ts\",\"tests/service/server/archive-api.test.ts\",\"tests/fixtures/archive.ts\"],\"requirementIds\":[\"AC-1.4\",\"AC-6.1\",\"AC-6.2\"],\"recommendedFixScope\":\"fresh-fix-path\",\"blocking\":true}],\"nonBlockingFindings\":[{\"id\":\"placeholder-execution-production-path\",\"severity\":\"major\",\"title\":\"The default execution lane is still a placeholder path\",\"evidence\":\"`apps/platform/server/services/processes/environment/script-execution.service.ts` still builds the repo-wide \\\"default execution payload,\\\" writes a \\\"Default Execution Summary,\\\" and reports \\\"Execution placeholder completed...\\\" while emitting only a single `process_event`. That is a material non-real production path for this epic because the archive is being exercised primarily against placeholder runtime output rather than real process-type execution.\",\"affectedFiles\":[\"apps/platform/server/services/processes/environment/script-execution.service.ts\"],\"requirementIds\":[],\"recommendedFixScope\":\"human-ruling\",\"blocking\":false}],\"unresolvedItems\":[\"A new finalized runtime-object contract is still needed if the archive is supposed to capture `reasoning`, `script_emission`, `tool_call`, and `tool_result` without collapsing back to presentation history rows.\",\"The implementation still needs a concrete producer for `relatedArtifactVersionId` and `relatedSourceProvenanceId` during finalization; the current codebase only implements the read-side enrichment.\",\"No executable end-to-end archive/browser suite currently runs because `test:e2e` is scaffold-only in the epic gate.\"],\"gateResult\":\"pass\"}]},\"errors\":[{\"code\":\"PROVIDER_UNAVAILABLE\",\"message\":\"Provider execution failed for claude-code.\"}],\"warnings\":[],\"artifacts\":[{\"kind\":\"result-envelope\",\"path\":\"/Users/leemoore/code/liminal-build/docs/spec-build/v2/epics/07--archive-and-derived-views/artifacts/epic/001-epic-verifier-batch.json\"}],\"startedAt\":\"2026-05-05T08:27:04.301Z\",\"finishedAt\":\"2026-05-05T08:36:30.487Z\"}\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/07--archive-and-derived-views/artifacts/epic/004-epic-verifier-batch.json:1:{\"command\":\"epic-verify\",\"version\":1,\"status\":\"ok\",\"outcome\":\"revise\",\"result\":{\"outcome\":\"revise\",\"verifierResults\":[{\"resultId\":\"0f1389f1-9f92-440f-9468-99f1079eb569\",\"outcome\":\"pass\",\"provider\":\"codex\",\"model\":\"gpt-5.4\",\"reviewerLabel\":\"epic-verifier-1\",\"crossStoryFindings\":[\"Stories 1-7 are wired end to end through shared archive contracts, Convex archive tables, Fastify archive routes, execution finalization hooks, and the client archive/turn/derived-view surfaces.\",\"Archive-entry degradation now propagates consistently into turn and derived-view rebuilds via shared enrichment, so detached or missing provenance no longer degrades only the archive page.\",\"Long-history behavior diverges across surfaces: archive entries and turns expose bounded paging, but derived views truncate after 50 items with no continuation signal.\"],\"architectureFindings\":[\"The canonical separation is intact: live websocket/current-object history remains on the process work surface, while finalized archive writes flow through `ArchiveFinalizationService` into `archiveEntries`.\",\"Derived-view reads drift from the tech design's cursor-bounded read contract. The design calls for cursor pagination with a default derived-view limit, but the current API exposes no paging inputs and silently slices the computed set.\",\"The default production execution stack uses real Local and Daytona adapters, but the script layer is still one shared runtime-audit payload rather than process-type-specific execution logic.\"],\"epicCoverageAssessment\":[\"Both requested gates passed: `corepack pnpm run green-verify` and `corepack pnpm run verify-all`.\",\"Automated happy-path coverage is strong across Convex, server, client, and integration tests for archive persistence, finalization, read/reopen, turn derivation, derived views, and provenance degradation.\",\"Gate coverage still has explicit gaps: `guard:no-test-changes` and `test:e2e` are scaffold-only `SKIP` scripts, so there is still no executable browser/runtime end-to-end archive scenario enforced by automation.\"],\"productionPathFindings\":[\"No fake provider adapter is wired into the default production registry: `DefaultProviderAdapterRegistry` resolves real Local and Daytona adapters, while `SingleAdapterRegistry` and `InMemoryProviderAdapter` stay test-only.\",\"The remaining non-real execution-path concern is the shared `buildIntegratedRuntimeAuditPayload` path, which generates a generic workspace-inspection run for every execution instead of process-type-specific runtime logic.\",\"No fake archive store or shim route was found in the archive read/write path itself; archive persistence still flows through Fastify services and `PlatformStore` into Convex.\"],\"blockingFindings\":[],\"nonBlockingFindings\":[{\"id\":\"EV-ARCHIVE-001\",\"severity\":\"major\",\"title\":\"Derived archive views are hard-capped at 50 with no pagination contract\",\"evidence\":\"Flow 7 says archive entries, turns, and derived views use cursor pagination with default limits, including derived views at a default of 50 (`docs/spec-build/v2/epics/07--archive-and-derived-views/tech-design.md:668-674`). The derived-view route exposes no paging query (`apps/platform/server/schemas/archive.ts:37-44`), the shared response has no page metadata (`apps/platform/shared/contracts/archive.ts:282-285`), and the service simply `slice(0, 50)`s computed views (`apps/platform/server/services/archive/derived-archive-view.service.ts:210-211`). Once a process has more than 33 turns, some `turn_range`/`chunk_candidate` views become unreachable with no `hasMore` signal.\",\"affectedFiles\":[\"apps/platform/server/schemas/archive.ts\",\"apps/platform/shared/contracts/archive.ts\",\"apps/platform/server/services/archive/derived-archive-view.service.ts\",\"docs/spec-build/v2/epics/07--archive-and-derived-views/tech-design.md\"],\"requirementIds\":[\"AC-7.3\"],\"recommendedFixScope\":\"fresh-fix-path\",\"blocking\":false},{\"id\":\"EV-ARCHIVE-002\",\"severity\":\"observation\",\"title\":\"Production execution still runs through one shared runtime-audit payload\",\"evidence\":\"`createApp` constructs `new ScriptExecutionService(providerAdapterRegistry)` by default (`apps/platform/server/app.ts:285-286`). `ScriptExecutionService` then always builds `buildIntegratedRuntimeAuditPayload(...)` unless a custom factory is injected (`apps/platform/server/services/processes/environment/script-execution.service.ts:298-356`). That payload emits a generic workspace-inspection run with fixed archive/tool/model/process shapes (`apps/platform/server/services/processes/environment/script-execution.service.ts:18-295`). This is not a fake provider path, but it is still a generic execution path rather than process-type-specific runtime logic.\",\"affectedFiles\":[\"apps/platform/server/app.ts\",\"apps/platform/server/services/processes/environment/script-execution.service.ts\",\"apps/platform/server/services/processes/environment/provider-adapter-registry.ts\"],\"requirementIds\":[],\"recommendedFixScope\":\"human-ruling\",\"blocking\":false},{\"id\":\"EV-ARCHIVE-003\",\"severity\":\"observation\",\"title\":\"Story and epic gate commands still include scaffold-only checks\",\"evidence\":\"`guard:no-test-changes` only prints `SKIP: guard:no-test-changes not implemented for this repo yet` and `test:e2e` only prints `SKIP: test:e2e scaffolded in Story 0; no executable suite yet` (`package.json:23-27`). `green-verify` and `verify-all` passed, but those gate legs are not yet enforcing the intended protections.\",\"affectedFiles\":[\"package.json\"],\"requirementIds\":[],\"recommendedFixScope\":\"fresh-fix-path\",\"blocking\":false}],\"unresolvedItems\":[\"Decide whether the shared runtime-audit payload is an accepted interim production path or should be replaced before archive contents are treated as fully domain-real.\",\"Decide whether derived-view reads should implement the cursor pagination promised in the tech design, or whether the spec should explicitly bless a hard 50-view cap.\",\"Replace the scaffolded `guard:no-test-changes` and `test:e2e` scripts if those protections are required for future epic gates.\"],\"gateResult\":\"pass\"},{\"resultId\":\"248e7434-61cf-4b4c-ad96-75eaa7b37f05\",\"outcome\":\"revise\",\"provider\":\"codex\",\"model\":\"gpt-5.4\",\"reviewerLabel\":\"epic-verifier-2\",\"crossStoryFindings\":[\"Stories 2, 6, and 7 drift together on checkpoint-bound archive material: finalized runtime entries that need artifact/source linkage are withheld from the canonical archive until a later async checkpoint phase, so the archive can be incomplete immediately after execution completes.\",\"Stories 4, 5, and 7 are wired end-to-end, but the turn/view surfaces behave like rebuilders instead of cached bounded readers: every GET re-derives from the full archive, and derived views stop at the first 50 records with no way to read the remainder.\"],\"architectureFindings\":[\"Tech-design Q7/Flow 6 says archive rows should store nullable related ids and stay readable even when related context is unavailable; the implementation instead defers some rows until checkpoint provenance resolves.\",\"Tech-design Q5/Q8 says cached turns and derived views exist to keep long reads bounded, but the current read path full-scans and rewrites caches on every request and omits derived-view pagination altogether.\"],\"epicCoverageAssessment\":[\"Most Epic 7 behaviors are implemented and covered by passing automation: canonical archive taxonomy, idempotent append, authenticated archive/turn/view routes, provenance enrichment, degraded-entry rendering, and reload/reopen flows all have automated coverage.\",\"Coverage is weak around the completion-to-checkpoint window: the orchestrator tests explicitly poll for deferred archive rows to appear later, which means the suite does not prove immediate canonical visibility for all finalized entries.\",\"Long-process coverage proves a hard cap of 50 derived views, but it does not prove a contract for paging through the full derived-view set.\"],\"productionPathFindings\":[\"Production createApp wiring uses the real Convex store, Local/Daytona provider registry, and Octokit checkpoint writer; the in-memory stores/adapters remain test seams rather than the live execution path.\",\"The material production-path gap is the async checkpoint bridge: some finalized archive rows are only appended after background checkpoint work finishes, so canonical archive completeness depends on a later phase instead of the completion boundary itself.\"],\"blockingFindings\":[{\"id\":\"epic7-deferred-archive-append-window\",\"severity\":\"major\",\"title\":\"Checkpoint-bound archive entries are not appended at finalization time\",\"evidence\":\"`ProcessEnvironmentService.applyExecutionResultSideEffects` diverts any runtime archive entry with `artifactCheckpointIndex` or `sourceProvenanceBinding` into `deferredArchiveEntries` instead of appending it immediately (`apps/platform/server/services/processes/environment/process-environment.service.ts:731-735,1789-1790`). In the normal production path, successful execution then schedules `runCheckpointAsync` and returns without appending those rows (`apps/platform/server/services/processes/environment/process-environment.service.ts:644-662`). The actual append happens later inside checkpoint execution (`apps/platform/server/services/processes/environment/process-environment.service.ts:1024-1031,1108-1115`). The orchestration test has to poll until `script:live-archive-1` eventually appears, proving the row is not immediately durable after completion (`tests/service/server/process-execution-orchestrator.test.ts:731-749`). This leaves a crash/reload window where finalized material is missing from the canonical archive.\",\"affectedFiles\":[\"apps/platform/server/services/processes/environment/process-environment.service.ts\",\"tests/service/server/process-execution-orchestrator.test.ts\"],\"requirementIds\":[\"AC-1.4b\",\"AC-3.2a\",\"AC-3.2b\",\"AC-7.1a\"],\"recommendedFixScope\":\"fresh-fix-path\",\"blocking\":true},{\"id\":\"epic7-bounded-read-contract-drift\",\"severity\":\"major\",\"title\":\"Turn and derived-view reads do not implement the bounded cached-read contract\",\"evidence\":\"`DefaultTurnDerivationService.getTurns` always calls `rebuildTurns` before serving any page (`apps/platform/server/services/archive/turn-derivation.service.ts:81-98`), and `rebuildTurns` always full-scans the archive via `listAllArchiveEntries` before rewriting the entire turn cache (`apps/platform/server/services/archive/turn-derivation.service.ts:54-69,102-124`). `DefaultDerivedArchiveViewService.listViews` likewise rebuilds turns and rewrites derived views on every GET (`apps/platform/server/services/archive/derived-archive-view.service.ts:61-74`). After rebuilding, the service hard-slices the derived-view set to 50 (`apps/platform/server/services/archive/derived-archive-view.service.ts:25,66,210-211`), while the shared contract and route schema expose no cursor or page metadata for derived views (`apps/platform/shared/contracts/archive.ts:282-289`,`apps/platform/server/schemas/archive.ts:37-46`). The client can only report how many structural views it got, with no affordance to fetch omitted results (`apps/platform/client/features/processes/derived-archive-views-section.ts:46-49`).\",\"affectedFiles\":[\"apps/platform/server/services/archive/turn-derivation.service.ts\",\"apps/platform/server/services/archive/derived-archive-view.service.ts\",\"apps/platform/shared/contracts/archive.ts\",\"apps/platform/server/schemas/archive.ts\",\"apps/platform/client/features/processes/derived-archive-views-section.ts\"],\"requirementIds\":[\"TD-Q5\",\"TD-Q8\",\"AC-7.1b\",\"AC-7.3a\"],\"recommendedFixScope\":\"fresh-fix-path\",\"blocking\":true}],\"nonBlockingFindings\":[],\"unresolvedItems\":[\"The first `corepack pnpm run green-verify` run failed once in `tests/service/server/process-live-updates.test.ts:1397`, but a full rerun of `green-verify` and `verify-all` passed. I could not determine whether that was a timing flake or a one-off environment hiccup.\",\"I did not execute the manual live-service checklist with `pnpm run convex:dev` and `pnpm dev`; conclusions are based on code review plus automated gate runs.\"],\"gateResult\":\"pass\"}]},\"errors\":[],\"warnings\":[],\"artifacts\":[{\"kind\":\"result-envelope\",\"path\":\"/Users/leemoore/code/liminal-build/docs/spec-build/v2/epics/07--archive-and-derived-views/artifacts/epic/004-epic-verifier-batch.json\"}],\"startedAt\":\"2026-05-05T10:54:22.290Z\",\"finishedAt\":\"2026-05-05T11:06:10.055Z\"}\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
