{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_7","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"for f in docs/spec-build/v2/epics/07--archive-and-derived-views/artifacts/epic/00*-epic-verifier-batch.json; do echo '---' \"'$f; jq -r '\"'.result.verifierResults[] | \\\"reviewer=\\\\(.reviewerLabel) outcome=\\\\(.outcome) gate=\\\\(.gateResult)\\\\nblocking:\\\\n\\\" + ((.blockingFindings // []) | map(\\\"- [\\\\(.severity)] \\\\(.id): \\\\(.title)\\\") | join(\\\"\\\\n\\\")) + \\\"\\\\nnonblocking:\\\\n\\\" + ((.nonBlockingFindings // []) | map(\\\"- [\\\\(.severity)] \\\\(.id): \\\\(.title)\\\") | join(\\\"\\\\n\\\")) + \\\"\\\\nunresolved:\\\\n\\\" + ((.unresolvedItems // []) | map(\\\"- \\\" + .) | join(\\\"\\\\n\\\")) + \\\"\\\\n\\\"' \\\"\"'$f\"; done'","aggregated_output":"--- docs/spec-build/v2/epics/07--archive-and-derived-views/artifacts/epic/001-epic-verifier-batch.json\nreviewer=epic-verifier-1 outcome=block gate=pass\nblocking:\n- [critical] archive-taxonomy-production-gap: The shipped archive pipeline cannot emit four of the seven required canonical entry kinds\n- [major] archive-provenance-write-gap: Live archive writes never attach artifact-version or source-provenance references\nnonblocking:\n- [major] placeholder-execution-production-path: The default execution lane is still a placeholder path\nunresolved:\n- A new finalized runtime-object contract is still needed if the archive is supposed to capture `reasoning`, `script_emission`, `tool_call`, and `tool_result` without collapsing back to presentation history rows.\n- The implementation still needs a concrete producer for `relatedArtifactVersionId` and `relatedSourceProvenanceId` during finalization; the current codebase only implements the read-side enrichment.\n- No executable end-to-end archive/browser suite currently runs because `test:e2e` is scaffold-only in the epic gate.\n\n--- docs/spec-build/v2/epics/07--archive-and-derived-views/artifacts/epic/002-epic-verifier-batch.json\nreviewer=epic-verifier-1 outcome=block gate=pass\nblocking:\n- [critical] EV-E7-001: Live execution cannot emit the Epic 7 archive taxonomy\n- [major] EV-E7-002: Archive rows never capture artifact/source provenance on the live path\nnonblocking:\n- [minor] EV-E7-003: Process work surface never exposes an archive entry point\nunresolved:\n- `verify-all` passed, but `test:e2e` is scaffold-only and `guard:no-test-changes` is not implemented, so those gate layers remain unproven.\n- This review did not manually run `pnpm run convex:dev` and `pnpm dev` to validate archive generation against a live backend/provider session.\n\nreviewer=epic-verifier-2 outcome=block gate=pass\nblocking:\n- [critical] EV-07-001: The shipped archive write path never produces four of the seven required canonical entry kinds\n- [major] EV-07-002: Archive provenance coherence is unreachable on the real write path because archive rows never record related artifact/source ids\nnonblocking:\n- [major] EV-07-003: Source provenance enrichment can falsely degrade older archive entries because it only loads the newest 200 provenance rows\n- [major] EV-07-004: Turn and derived-view reads bypass the cached-projection design and rescan the full archive on every request\nunresolved:\n- The 2-second performance NFR for turn/archive reads at 5,000 archive entries was not measured against a real Convex-backed runtime during this review.\n- Manual end-to-end verification with `pnpm run convex:dev` and `pnpm dev` was not performed; production-path conclusions are based on code inspection plus automated test results.\n\n--- docs/spec-build/v2/epics/07--archive-and-derived-views/artifacts/epic/003-epic-verifier-batch.json\nreviewer=epic-verifier-1 outcome=block gate=pass\nblocking:\n- [critical] EV-ARCHIVE-001: Production executions still archive placeholder output instead of real process work\n- [major] EV-ARCHIVE-002: Deferred archive entries are silently dropped when provenance or checkpoint relations cannot be resolved\nnonblocking:\n- [observation] EV-ARCHIVE-003: Turn and derived-view reads bypass the intended cache-first bounded-read design\nunresolved:\n- Decide whether the placeholder execution payload is an explicit temporary stopgap or an unintended leftover from Epic 3; either way it should not ship as canonical archive truth.\n- No executable e2e suite currently verifies the browser/runtime archive flow because `test:e2e` is scaffold-only.\n\nreviewer=epic-verifier-2 outcome=block gate=pass\nblocking:\n- [critical] EV-001: Deferred archive entries are silently dropped when related artifact or source provenance cannot be resolved\n- [major] EV-002: Turn and derived-view rebuilds ignore related-context degradation computed by archive reads\n- [major] EV-003: Archive reopen bypasses source-provenance degradation logic for detached or revoked sources\nnonblocking:\n- [minor] EV-004: Derived-view reads are bounded but not cursor-paginated as designed\n- [major] EV-005: Production execution still runs through a placeholder default script payload\nunresolved:\n- `green-verify` and `verify-all` both passed, but `guard:no-test-changes` currently prints `SKIP`, so the story gate's extra protection is scaffolded rather than enforced.\n- Whether the placeholder default execution payload is accepted temporary debt outside Epic 7 needs an explicit product/architecture ruling before treating the archive path as production-real.\n\n--- docs/spec-build/v2/epics/07--archive-and-derived-views/artifacts/epic/004-epic-verifier-batch.json\nreviewer=epic-verifier-1 outcome=pass gate=pass\nblocking:\n\nnonblocking:\n- [major] EV-ARCHIVE-001: Derived archive views are hard-capped at 50 with no pagination contract\n- [observation] EV-ARCHIVE-002: Production execution still runs through one shared runtime-audit payload\n- [observation] EV-ARCHIVE-003: Story and epic gate commands still include scaffold-only checks\nunresolved:\n- Decide whether the shared runtime-audit payload is an accepted interim production path or should be replaced before archive contents are treated as fully domain-real.\n- Decide whether derived-view reads should implement the cursor pagination promised in the tech design, or whether the spec should explicitly bless a hard 50-view cap.\n- Replace the scaffolded `guard:no-test-changes` and `test:e2e` scripts if those protections are required for future epic gates.\n\nreviewer=epic-verifier-2 outcome=revise gate=pass\nblocking:\n- [major] epic7-deferred-archive-append-window: Checkpoint-bound archive entries are not appended at finalization time\n- [major] epic7-bounded-read-contract-drift: Turn and derived-view reads do not implement the bounded cached-read contract\nnonblocking:\n\nunresolved:\n- The first `corepack pnpm run green-verify` run failed once in `tests/service/server/process-live-updates.test.ts:1397`, but a full rerun of `green-verify` and `verify-all` passed. I could not determine whether that was a timing flake or a one-off environment hiccup.\n- I did not execute the manual live-service checklist with `pnpm run convex:dev` and `pnpm dev`; conclusions are based on code review plus automated gate runs.\n\n--- docs/spec-build/v2/epics/07--archive-and-derived-views/artifacts/epic/005-epic-verifier-batch.json\nreviewer=epic-verifier-1 outcome=block gate=fail\nblocking:\n- [critical] EPIC7-DERIVED-VIEW-PAGINATION-ROLLUP: Derived-view pagination refactor is incomplete and breaks the epic gate\n- [major] EPIC7-STale-DERIVED-CACHE-PRODUCTION: Convex production reads can return stale turns and derived views after new archive entries arrive\n- [major] EPIC7-SYNTHETIC-ARCHIVE-PRODUCTION-PATH: The default production archive capture path still archives a canned runtime-audit script, not real process execution\nnonblocking:\n\nunresolved:\n- Rerun `corepack pnpm run green-verify` and `corepack pnpm run verify-all` after finishing the derived-view pagination rollout; the current review could not observe any post-typecheck test result